33.2],[44.4,33.3],[44.2,34.1],[43.7,34.9],[43.2,35.5],[43.1,36.3],[42.3,37.2],[38,37.3]],"basis":"User pre-conquest display restriction between the rivers. Lower western edge follows retained Natural Earth Euphrates vertices; west-bank desert, joined river below Qurna and north Gulf coast remain allowed. Opens from630. Hatra is the sole northern ruling-elite exception."}],"destinationColourFrom":630,"neutralColour":"#9a7848","maxUnmatchedAnnualShare":0.025,"sources":[{"id":"LEDGER-CYPRUS","title":"Republic of Cyprus, The Maronites of Cyprus","url":"https://publications.gov.cy/assets/user/publications/2012/2012_389/MARONITES_2012_EN.pdf","basis":"Government account places early appearance in 686 and later waves in the Crusader era; reconstructed migration quantities use household priors, not a claim of uniformly Arabic-speaking identity in 686."},{"id":"LEDGER-THUGHUR","title":"The Byzantine conquest of Cilicia and the Hamdanids of Aleppo, 959–965","url":"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/anatolian-studies/article/abs/byzantine-conquest-of-cilicia-and-the-hamdanids-of-aleppo-959965/5C9F862B3ADFB1C123A58AB76F6BD157","basis":"Cilician reconquest culminates in 965; the broad 934–980 withdrawal and named tribal mixture follow the user display reconstruction. Not a second copy of Caucasus garrisons."}],"basis":"One standing-population ledger: 500,000 initial household-equivalent people in the northwest homeland (100,000 households ×5); 450,000 are allocated once to early regional inflows, with 50,000 initially unallocated. Initial/early reservoir priors were raised after the smaller model required rapid growth. Other reservoirs begin empty. All journeys transfer people; no independent origin or presence spawns. One common intrinsic logistic natural-growth rate is fitted against departures; stated regional capacities are visualization priors, not historical carrying-capacity measurements. Closed elite/garrison roster cohorts do not generate inferred descendants."}
